{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And I said to them, Whoever has gold.</b> I set the matter so as to be preventable, for there was no gold ready at hand." "<b>They broke it off and gave it to me.</b> And they volunteered the gold in haste." "<b>And I cast it into the fire.</b> I sought to delay the matter, and I cast the gold into the fire without the metallurgical procedures required to melt gold." "<b>And out came this calf.</b> Without any effort of mine; and they did not wait for me to make it as they had demanded. For though it says וַיַּעֲשֵׂהוּ עֵגֶל מַסֵּכָה, this was not said of Aaron; rather, the desire of the people made the maker do it, in the manner of וְסָמַךְ אֶת יָדוֹ וְשָׁחַט (Leviticus 3:8) — the desire of the one offering pressed his hand, and the one slaughtering slaughtered. And so He testified in saying אֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ אֶת הָעֵגֶל אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה אַהֲרֹן — that they made the calf in which Aaron's act was done, in that he engraved a form and cast the gold into the fire."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:49.080750693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}